r-discussed) and maybe D. She can either maintain vote for C or shift. She should bring in evidence about A and D, compare with C, and maybe suggest next steps. She should state her current recommendation. Likely maintain C but note need to discuss D as well. Provide explicit facts: A anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. D responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, moody, loner. Also note concerns about A: unfriendly (crew cooperation), eats unhealthily (maybe health but not criteria). D: moody, loner (crew cooperation). Also D's hot temper, know-it-all (communication). So Emily can argue that while A has strong technical and anticipation, the unfriendly nature and unorganized aspects (not in her notes but she has \"sometimes not good at taking criticism\" from earlier) affect crew cooperation and adaptability. D has strong problem solving and responsibility but moody and loner affect crew cooperation and communication. So C remains best despite communication issues. She can propose to discuss D next. So she will maintain vote for C.\n\nThus produce public message: agree with Sarah, maintain C, note A's strengths but concerns, note D's strengths but concerns, propose to discuss D next. Then metadata JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
